Z||000008||Bruce||01-24-2000||06:28 PM||||So much for that idea: I wasn't aware that the Flowmaster installation is such an ordeal. While my muffler guy said he would be happy to take the money that the two hours of modifications it would take to make the muffler fit, he advised it would be a lot of $ for nothing more than a lot more noise. I think I'll bank that labor time for manifold porting and reinforcement.<BR>Hope I can get my money back on the muffler....hope my experience helps someone else!!||||reg||1
Z||000009||WKDFIRO||01-24-2000||08:01 PM||||Its worth it!!!!!! The flowmaster that we use is the same as the firebird/camaro. Yes there is modifications but buying a Flowmaster for quietness is like buying a Viper to go to the market. It sounds very cool to go in. Modifications shouldn't be that much money for what they are going to do to it. You will love the noise you will get out of the flowmaster. If you want quiet than send it back.<BR>It would take no more than hour to make the modifications, weld it up. Shop around!||||reg||4
Z||000010||Bruce||01-24-2000||08:58 PM||||Does it do as advertised: improve performance and gas mileage?||||reg||1
Z||000011||DXR_DAD||01-24-2000||09:11 PM||||Bruce, as we talked about before this exhaust upgrade thing is not cheap. Check the price of the Ocelot system......$269.96+Labor. And from what I've heard it's not that great.<BR>So I'm sure it's not as good as a flowmaster. Sometimes we just have to bite the bullet and dig in the pockets and Pay! Pay! Pay!. 2 hours labor doesn't seem to bad???||||reg||11
Z||000012||Bruce||01-24-2000||09:38 PM||||Thanks, Bill<BR>I'll call your guy at Golden Gate Muffler and see what he says. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||stimpy||01-24-2000||11:21 PM||||I have the Flowmaster and low restrictn cat on my GT and believe me, it does make a difference.  I also use the Camaro model along with 3.5" pipe. It is a VERY TIGHT fit. In fact the left pipe exits about 1/2" lower. I am using flat oval Megs tips and it is not very noticeable due to the skills of the guys at Tracy Muffler in Tracy CA. (Those guys are the BEST!) The car seems to have a LOT more grunt and sounds great.  Remember, loud pipes save lives! ||||reg||1
